entions: "If something chases the tiger then it visits the dog.".\n   - This statement does not directly tell us whether the tiger chases the lion or not.\n\n4.**Analyze the relationship between visiting and chasing the lion:**.\n   - The context mentions: "If something visits the lion then it likes the squirrel.".\n   - This statement does not directly tell us whether the tiger chases the lion or not.\n\n5.**Analyze the relationship between being red and chasing the tiger:**.\n   - The context mentions: "If something is red and it chases the tiger then it likes the squirrel.".All the statements clearly indicate that the tiger does not chase the lion.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
