ething is small then it is hot, Anne must be hot.\n- Since Anne is hot and smooth, and if something is hot and smooth then it is black, Anne must be black (which is consistent with the previous information).\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Bob is round":\n- Bob is small and not round.\n- According to statement 4, if something is not round and small then it is yellow.\n- Since Bob is small and not round, Bob must be yellow.\n- According to statement 1, all yellow things are black.\n- Therefore, Bob must be black.\n- Since Bob is small and black, and if something is small then it is hot, Bob must be hot.\n- According to statement 7, if something is hot then it is not red.\n- Therefore, Bob must not be red.\n- Since Bob is small, not round, black, and hot, the statement "Bob is round" is true.\n\nThus, the correct answer is: B. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
