ion.\n- The squirrel is not green or rough.\n- The tiger is smooth.\n\n3.**Ignore the implications:**.\n- Since the squirrel is green, it can also be blue (because if something is blue, it avoids the lion, and the squirrel is green, so it can avoid the lion).\n- The squirrel avoids the tiger because it is smooth (since smooth things are small, and the squirrel is smooth, it can avoid the tiger).\n\n4.**Inconclusive Result:**.\n- The squirrel can be blue even though it is green\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
