Something Sees Bald Eagle, Then Bald Eagle Sees Rabbit**: This is given directly.\n13.**If Something Needs Dog, Then Dog Sees Rabbit**: This is given directly.\n14.**If Something Needs Dog and Dog is Kind, Then Dog Chases Rabbit**: This is given directly.\n15.**If Something Needs Rabbit and Rabbit is Blue, Then Rabbit Sees Bald Eagle**: This is given directly.\n16.**If Something Sees Rabbit and Rabbit Sees Lion, Then It is Kind**: This is given directly.\n17.**If Lion is Rough and Lion Needs Rabbit, Then Lion is Kind**: This is given directly.\n18.**If Something Sees Bald Eagle, Then Bald Eagle Needs Dog**: This is given directly.\n19.**If Something Sees Rabbit, Then Rabbit Sees Dog**: This is given directly.If the rabbit is kind, and the rabbit chases the dog, then the bald eagle is mean and does not need the dog.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
