for some purpose.\n\n8.**The lion visits the squirrel.**.\n   - This means the lion has interacted with the squirrel.\n\n9.**The squirrel likes the lion.**.\n   - This indicates that the squirrel has a preference for the lion.\n\n10.**If something needs the mouse and it needs the lion then the lion needs the mouse.**.\n    - This is a logical implication that if an entity requires both the mouse and the lion, then the lion must also require the mouse.\n\n11.**If something visits the lion then it needs the cat.**.\n    - This means that if an entity visits the lion, it must also visit the cat.\n\n12.**If the mouse visits the squirrel then the squirrel likes the cat.**.\n    - This implies that if the mouse visits the squirrel, the squirrel must also like the cat.\n\n13.**If something is rough then it is cold.The squirrel is not cold, which means the squirrel does not need to visit the cat.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
